+        final String newTagVal = context.getProperty(TAG_VALUE).evaluateAttributeExpressions(flowFile).getValue();
+
+        if(!context.getProperty(APPEND_TAG).asBoolean()) {
+            flowFile = session.removeAllAttributes(flowFile, Pattern.compile("^s3\\.tag\\..*"));

 Review comment:
   I think we should remove existing FlowFile S3 attributes earlier regardless of the `APPEND_TAG` value. Then populate FlowFile attributes using the latest `tags` list at `onTrigger` method.

   Current code assumes that the incoming FlowFile has the latest S3 tag attributes. But in case tags are updated elsewhere, the ones retrieved by `GetObjectTaggingRequest` is more reliable.

   Also, current code calculates tagKey and tagValue twice. This can be avoided by populating FlowFile attributes from `tags` list at `onTrigger` method.

