column359:
16/Jan/19 10:33;ivera;I had a quick look and my guess is that this is a case where we are indexing big lines and the resulting BKD tree is not optimal and we are ending up checking most of the shapes when querying. This is actually interesting because we might need to break big lines to prevent this situations. Reproducing line:
{code:java}
ant test  -Dtestcase=TestLatLonLineShapeies -Dtests.seed=37C511586778964F -Dtests.multiplier=2 -Dtests.nightly=true -Dtests.slow=true -Dtests.linedocsfile=/home/jenkins/jenkins-slave/workspace/Lucene-Solr-NightlyTests-8.x/test-data/enwiki.random.lines.txt -Dtests.locale=und -Dtests.timezone=Asia/Chungking -Dtests.asserts=true -Dtests.file.encoding=UTF-8
{code}

