 Review comment:
   Nope! `std::string` is not null terminated. The `const char *` passed into the construct is null terminated it effectively results in `char[strlen(cstr)] chars; memcpy(chars, cstr, strlen(cstr));` (obviously not C++ code, just an illustration).

