+      StreamObserver<ConstructionApi.ConstructionResponse> responseObserver) {
+    try {
+      responseObserver.onNext(construct(request));
+      responseObserver.onCompleted();
+    } catch (RuntimeException exn) {
+      responseObserver.onError(exn);
+      throw exn;
+    }
+  }
+
+  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
+    int port = Integer.parseInt(args[0]);
+    System.out.println("Starting construction service at localhost:" + port);

 Review comment:
   It has a different lifecycle. An SDK may know about certain transforms and start up services on its own to expand them (in which case it'd probably be part of some WrapperTransform's expand method). 

