+      LOG.warn(
+          "Executor service was not properly shutdown after {} attempts, trying to forcibly stop it.",
+          ATTEMPTS_TO_SHUTDOWN);
+      executorService.shutdownNow();

 Review comment:
   I think that we need to repeat the `awaitTermination` loop after forcible `shutdownNow`. It's possible that invoking `shutdown` won't have any effect within 30s timeout as it's not interrupting currently running tasks (that's why it wasn't originally used). So this approach won't interrupt the `readLoop` when it's waiting for Kinesis to return some records or when putting records to a full recordsQueue. But with additional waiting it should be fine.

