   If I had to guess at the var char problem, this doesn't look correct for handling nulls on arrays.   It seems that you want to explicitly set null instead of just skipping over the loop.  Looking at ListVector (quickly) I didn't see a method for doing this.  Looking at the java code-base it might be that the writer does have a way to do this (and might be better to use instead).  I.e. Somthing like listVector.getWriter() up top.  And then writeNull().  But I don't have a java dev environment setup so I can't give you specifics.  It might be worth asking about setting nulls on list vectors in general if pursuing this approach doesn't help.  (It might also pay to create a failing unit test if this is really causing issues.

